At run time, and only when the user runs or schedules the corresponding jobs,
JARVIS-1 downloads data from third-party publishers. That data is not
distributed with JARVIS-1 and remains subject to each publisher's terms:

  MITRE ATT&CK (c) The MITRE Corporation — https://attack.mitre.org/resources/legal-and-branding/terms-of-use/
  abuse.ch ThreatFox, MalwareBazaar, URLhaus, Feodo Tracker
  CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog
  Spamhaus DROP, OpenPhish, Proofpoint Emerging Threats, blocklist.de,
  CINS Army, Binary Defense, IPsum

The optional Exa, OpenAI and Resend integrations use the user's own API keys
and are governed by those services' terms.
